From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:41:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] CUDA: keep MX scale-byte selectors out of NVFP4 compact
 packages

Upstream-base: tile-ai/tilelang@2123e412ce2217b324c50c4ec967213906456ac5

Rationale: upstream #3286 added a shared-scale compact package route that
hardcodes both scale-byte selectors to zero. After adding MXFP8 (1X) and
MXFP4 (2X), dispatching either format through it silently repeats the wrong
scale bytes. Restrict this route to 4X; the MX formats retain their existing
per-MMA route and selectors. NVFP4 retains the upstream optimization.

Quality: required to preserve the deployed MX arithmetic on this newer
base. Add exact varying-scale products for both A and B, with K128 scales
1, 2, 4 and 8: the expected sum is 480 for unit operands.

Tests: source syntax and fresh patch application are checked locally.
The four new SM12x CUDA regression cases require target hardware and have
not been run for this candidate. See the deployment experiment receipts.

Upstream-status: local compatibility patch; no upstream PR as of 2026-11-04.
---
 ...elang_language_mxf8f6f4_mma_block_scale.py | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 ...tilelang_language_mxfp4_mma_block_scale.py | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../macro/mma_sm120_macro_generator.py        |  5 +++--
 3 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/testing/python/language/test_tilelang_language_mxf8f6f4_mma_block_scale.py b/testing/python/language/test_tilelang_language_mxf8f6f4_mma_block_scale.py
index e93935ab0..7c9d48a3c 100644
--- a/testing/python/language/test_tilelang_language_mxf8f6f4_mma_block_scale.py
+++ b/testing/python/language/test_tilelang_language_mxf8f6f4_mma_block_scale.py
@@ -180,6 +180,25 @@ def test_mxf8f6f4_rejects_compact_kmajor_scales():
         tilelang.lower(main, target=target, enable_device_compile=False)
 
 
+@tilelang.testing.requires_cuda
+@tilelang.testing.requires_cuda_compute_version_ge(12, 0)
+@tilelang.testing.requires_cuda_compute_version_lt(13, 0)
+@pytest.mark.parametrize("scaled_operand", ["a", "b"])
+def test_mxfp8_shared_scale_words_select_every_byte(scaled_operand):
+    """A K128 tile must consume all four bytes, not repeat the first scale."""
+    import torch
+
+    a = torch.ones((64, 128), device="cuda", dtype=torch.float8_e4m3fn)
+    b = torch.ones_like(a)
+    scales = torch.tensor([127, 128, 129, 130], device="cuda", dtype=torch.uint8).repeat(64, 1)
+    sfa = scales if scaled_operand == "a" else torch.full_like(scales, 127)
+    sfb = scales if scaled_operand == "b" else torch.full_like(scales, 127)
+    kernel = tilelang.compile(_make_mxfp8_matmul_kernel(64, 64, 128), target="cuda", out_idx=[4])
+    out = kernel(a, b, sfa.view(torch.uint32), sfb.view(torch.uint32))
+    # 32 products at each of scales 1, 2, 4, 8; all products and sums are exact.
+    torch.testing.assert_close(out, torch.full((64, 64), 480.0, device="cuda"), rtol=0, atol=0)
+
+
